    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "まい can express the intention not to do something or a negative deduction, depending on the person and the context.",
     "texto": [
      "It is a written or solemn form. With a first-person subject it usually shows intention; with a statement about another event it can be an inference. It is not a neutral everyday negation.",
      "同じ 失敗 は 二度 と 繰り返す まい。 (I won't repeat the same mistake again.)",
      "この 量 では、今日 中 に 終わる まい。 (With this amount, it probably won't finish today.)"
     ],
